  <section id="recovery-engine" class="reactivation-engine-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">The CallTeam Lead Recovery Engine</div>
      <h2>A structured system for finding what is still commercially useful.</h2>
      <p class="reactivation-section-intro">We do not dump every old record into a dialer. The history, fit, data condition and reason to reconnect shape what happens next.</p>
      <div class="reactivation-engine-panel">
        <div class="reactivation-engine-head"><span><i></i> RECOVERY WORKFLOW</span><strong>SEVEN CONTROLLED STAGES</strong></div>
        <div class="reactivation-engine-grid">
          <article><small>01</small><strong>Audit the lead pool</strong><p>Review sources, stages, age, notes, ownership, previous activity and obvious exclusions.</p></article>
          <article><small>02</small><strong>Clean the records</strong><p>Remove unusable entries, identify data gaps, check contacts and prepare the required campaign fields.</p></article>
          <article><small>03</small><strong>Segment and prioritize</strong><p>Group leads by fit, source, history, timing, value, data confidence and the likely reason to reconnect.</p></article>
          <article class="active"><small>04</small><strong>Build the message</strong><p>Prepare the context, call opening, business reason, questions, proof, objections and next step.</p></article>
          <article><small>05</small><strong>Call and follow up</strong><p>Use human calling and approved supporting follow up to reach the right person and test what changed.</p></article>
          <article><small>06</small><strong>Qualify and book</strong><p>Confirm fit, role, reason, interest, timing and whether a useful sales conversation should happen.</p></article>
          <article><small>07</small><strong>Record and route</strong><p>Book, schedule later, refer, nurture, correct, close or remove the record with a clear reason.</p></article>
        </div>
        <div class="reactivation-engine-loop"><span>↻</span><strong>Every response improves the priorities, message, data and next round of follow up.</strong></div>
