  <section id="faq" class="reactivation-faq-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">B2B lead reactivation FAQ</div>
      <h2>Questions companies ask before working an old or neglected lead pool.</h2>
      <div class="reactivation-faq-list">
        <details><summary>What are B2B lead reactivation services?</summary><p>B2B lead reactivation services reconnect with old, dormant, unresponsive or neglected business leads. The work can include auditing and cleaning the data, segmenting the lead pool, preparing the message, human calling, structured follow up, qualification, appointment booking and recording a clear next action.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What is CRM lead reactivation?</summary><p>CRM lead reactivation is the process of identifying inactive contacts and opportunities inside a customer relationship management system, deciding which records still deserve attention, reconnecting with them and returning useful outcomes to the CRM.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What types of leads can CallTeam reactivate?</summary><p>CallTeam can work with old CRM leads, dormant opportunities, previous inquiries, unresponsive inbound leads, event and webinar contacts, past proposals, no decision opportunities, target accounts, referral lists and previous prospecting campaigns.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How old can a lead be?</summary><p>Age alone does not determine whether a lead is useful. Fit, source, previous engagement, data condition, reason for the original interest, timing and what may have changed all matter. CallTeam reviews the pool before recommending outreach.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can CallTeam follow up with inbound leads?</summary><p>Yes. CallTeam can contact inbound inquiries that were not reached, received incomplete follow up or went quiet after an initial response. The call should reflect what the person requested and how much time has passed.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can you reactivate event and webinar leads?</summary><p>Yes. CallTeam can work with conference attendees, booth visitors, webinar registrations, session participants and other event contacts. The outreach needs a specific reason tied to the event and the buyer rather than a generic follow up message.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can you work lost or no decision opportunities?</summary><p>Yes. Previous opportunities can be reviewed around the original problem, decision, objections, timing, stakeholders and outcome. The reactivation conversation tests what changed and whether another sales discussion is now useful.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does CallTeam use human callers?</summary><p>Yes. Experienced people handle live calls, listening, objections, referrals, qualification and next step decisions. AI and sales technology can support data organization, enrichment, segmentation, research, priorities and reporting.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is lead reactivation the same as cold calling?</summary><p>No. Cold calling commonly starts with a new prospect who may have no previous relationship with the company. Lead reactivation starts with a known record, previous interaction, earlier campaign or existing CRM history. Human calling can be part of both services, but the context and message are different.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is lead reactivation the same as lead generation?</summary><p>No. Lead generation identifies and creates possible new opportunities. Lead reactivation returns to contacts and opportunities that already exist. CallTeam can connect both when the company needs to recover the current database and build a new prospect list.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is lead reactivation the same as appointment setting?</summary><p>Lead reactivation focuses on recovering and correctly routing existing leads. Appointment setting focuses on qualifying and scheduling a sales conversation. A reactivation campaign can include appointment setting when a lead meets the agreed standard.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can CallTeam build a list if we do not have enough leads?</summary><p>Yes. CallTeam can clarify the ideal customer profile and build a targeted B2B prospect list using access to a global business contact universe with more than 300 million records. Records are selected, checked and prepared for the campaign rather than treated as automatically qualified leads.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does CallTeam own a database of 300 million contacts?</summary><p>CallTeam uses access to a global business contact universe with more than 300 million records. We do not present every record as owned, current or qualified. The relevant accounts and contacts must be selected, checked and prepared around the client campaign.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does CallTeam clean and enrich the lead data?</summary><p>CallTeam can review the lead pool for duplicates, missing fields, obvious bad data, role relevance, contact gaps and account context. The exact cleanup, validation and enrichment work depends on the source and campaign scope.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Which outreach channels are used?</summary><p>CallTeam is built around human calling. Approved email or other appropriate supporting follow up can be included depending on the lead source, available permissions, client process, market and engagement scope.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How does CallTeam qualify a reactivated lead?</summary><p>The standard is agreed before launch and can include account fit, role relevance, what changed, current business reason, interest, timing, decision path and a clear next step. Not every response should become a meeting.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can CallTeam book appointments from old leads?</summary><p>Yes. When a reactivated lead meets the qualification standard and accepts a relevant next conversation, CallTeam can schedule the appointment and provide the sales team with the account, contact, reason, context, timing, objections and agreed purpose.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can CallTeam work inside our CRM?</summary><p>CallTeam can work with an agreed CRM or structured campaign workflow when access, permissions, fields, ownership and operating rules are clear. Another reporting and handoff method can be used when direct access is not appropriate.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What happens when somebody is interested but not ready?</summary><p>The lead should receive a specific future action rather than being forced onto the calendar. That can include a follow up date, nurture route, additional information, another stakeholder or a condition that needs to change first.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What reporting will we receive?</summary><p>Reporting can include records worked, calls, connection outcomes, dispositions, objections, referrals, wrong contacts, data corrections, follow up dates, qualified leads, appointments and market patterns. The exact scorecard is agreed before launch.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How long does a lead reactivation campaign take?</summary><p>The timeline depends on record volume, data quality, lead age, number of segments, buyer seniority, calling workload, follow up depth, response rates and the amount of evidence required. CallTeam reviews the pool before defining the campaign.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How much do B2B lead reactivation services cost?</summary><p>Pricing depends on lead volume, data condition, lead age and source, research requirements, buyer seniority, calling workload, follow up depth, qualification complexity, CRM workflow, reporting and campaign duration.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does CallTeam guarantee recovered revenue or appointments?</summary><p>No honest provider controls the quality of every old record, the buyer, the offer, the market, the timing or what changed. CallTeam defines the process, performs the agreed work, reports the evidence and improves the campaign. Specific commercial commitments belong in the engagement agreement.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How do we start?</summary><p>Start with a strategy call. We review the offer, lead sources, record volume, data condition, available history, target buyer, qualification standard, CRM workflow, sales capacity and the outcome the campaign needs to produce.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

